<title>MEXICO: Hong Kong's VTech details Mexico plans.</title>
<headline>Hong Kong's VTech details Mexico plans.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong-based VTech Holdings Limited detailed Thursday plans to open a 40,000 square foot service plant in the western Mexican city of Guadalajara in the state of Jalisco.</p>
<p>The new plant, which is scheduled to be operational by August 1997, will entail a capital investment of $1.5 million, VTech said.</p>
<p>&quot;The plant's principle activity will be to provide maintenance and repair for VTech-brand cordless phones,&quot; the consumer electronics manufacturer said in a statement.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7287902))</p>
